Z||000000||Anthony||10-28-1999||08:45 PM||||I guess I should have mentioned my 86 has a ferarri 308 body conversion it has bell tech 2"drop spindles in the front.By the way the front sits perfect,and steers graet,no problems wondering,just a little bit of steering wheel shake over bumps but thats it.The rear looks like it sits a little bit higher than the front about an inch.It has been lowered 2" with modified bell tech springs.I have more fender room over the rear than the front.About an inch.That is why I was thinking about putting coil overs in the rear,I need to go 3" total from the stock highth.Not the 2" I already have.The front sits on 215-60-15 tires and the rear is on 225-60-15.Going to bigger tires in the rear will only take up the fender clearance but the back would still look higher.thanks for your help ||||reg||1
Z||000001||88 Fiero||10-28-1999||11:04 PM||||Anthony...I have a friend that has a 328 body on his Fiero...He got a 3 piece HRE wheels on it and the size of the wheels are 17 inch all around 4's....why hassle dropping your car to 3 inch lower where your going to ruin everything in the bottom...just invest some wheels and it will cover up much of the extra space...this is a common problem on kit cars...you get too much gap between the fenders and the tires...||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||10-28-1999||11:47 PM||||You ought to check out my discussion thread over in the general chat side called "Lower, firmer, tougher, meaner." LowCG explains that using the front strut housing from a Citation on the rear of a Fiero should drop the tail about an inch, that's about what you want, right? The coil overs are very nice, if you can afford them.||||reg||1
